course: dictionary
lesson: 9444
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Read the words around the word. «Picture Year 5's cake stall: parents baked the cakes for free» is about a table where things are sold, because cakes are sold at a stall.
explain: «The car stalled at the traffic lights» uses stall in a different way. The engine suddenly stopped working. The words around it, car and traffic lights, are your clue.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits. Put your meaning in place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense. In «Stop stalling!», the meaning is delaying, not selling, so the sentence is telling someone to stop wasting time.
fact: A stall can be a small table or stand where things are sold, like a market stall or a cake stall.
fact: A stall can also be a small space in a stable or barn for one animal, such as a horse or a cow.
fact: If an engine stalls, it suddenly stops working, often by mistake.
fact: To stall is to delay on purpose so you don't have to do something yet.
fact: In a theatre (UK), the stalls are the seats on the ground floor.
exercise: In «Picture Year 5's cake stall», what is a stall? | An engine that has stopped working | The seats on the ground floor of a theatre | A small space for a horse in a stable | *A table or stand where things are sold
exercise: «The car stalled at the traffic lights.» What has happened? | The car was repainted red | *The engine suddenly stopped working | The driver fell asleep at the wheel | The car drove very fast
exercise: «Stop stalling!» tells someone to... | Stop selling things at the market | Stop watching the play | *Stop wasting time and get on with it | Stop going into the stable
test: «The horse rested in its stall after the race.» What is a stall here? | A word that means to delay | A table where things are sold | The seats in a theatre | *A small space in a stable for one animal
test: «He stalled for time because he hadn't finished his homework.» What does stalled mean? | *Delayed on purpose | Sat in the stalls of a theatre | Sold things at a market | Stopped an engine by mistake
exam: 20 players pay 50p each at a fair game, so the stall takes £10, but it gives out £15 in prizes. Is the stall making a loss or a profit? | A profit of £5 | A profit of £15 | *A loss of £5 | A loss of £10
